{"agent":"U15","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new helper shells out to the `uv` CLI by bare name with `check=True` and no existence check, skip, or fallback: `subprocess.run([\"uv\", \"venv\", \"--quiet\", \"--seed\", \"--python\", sys.executable, str(path)], ...)`. On any host where `uv` is not on PATH — for example the very Ubuntu host with `python3.12-venv` split out that motivated this change, a distro build sandbox, or a developer who has installed the project's test extra but not the standalone `uv` binary — this raises `FileNotFoundError` immediately, and all three venv-based tests (`test_the_declared_dependency_is_actually_installed_by_the_wheel`, `test_installed_adopt_works_end_to_end`, `test_installed_mcp_server_completes_a_handshake`) error before the wheel is ever installed. The previous code only required the interpreter running the suite (`python -m venv`), so the change swaps one host-coupled prerequisite (ensurepip) for a different, undeclared one (the `uv` executable plus a seed step for `bin/pip`); the docstring's claim that the venv build \"does not depend on that\" is true only for ensurepip, not for the tool the tests now invoke. Nothing in this diff declares `uv` as a test dependency or guards the call with a skip/fallback, so the module can no longer be run on a plain Python host.","digest":"09d0c186be04bff6","location":"tests/test_packaging.py:`_clean_venv`","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_packaging.py:`_clean_venv`"}],"chunks_total":2,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":5792,"diff_sha":"1e47f4cc0695ab3491bd7e7a58f80d69edb1066c177475a52298b8d9778ee4c8","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":233.1,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek